MindSafe Vault
“Your Mind, Secured. Your Well-being, Monitored.”

A Privacy-Focused Mental Health Monitoring and Decision-Support System

Abstract

Mental health management among students requires both continuous monitoring and strict data privacy. Existing systems either lack intelligent analysis or fail to ensure confidentiality of sensitive user data, leading to reduced trust and ineffective usage.

This paper presents MindSafe Vault, a privacy-centric mental health monitoring platform that securely records user data and applies rule-based analytics to detect stress patterns and potential risks. The system follows a zero-knowledge approach, ensuring that all sensitive information remains encrypted and accessible only with user permission.

By combining secure storage, controlled access, and intelligent analysis, the platform enables safe, reliable, and proactive mental health monitoring while maintaining complete user control over personal data.

Keywords: Mental Health Monitoring, Data Security, Encryption, Decision Support System, Privacy Protection

