1. Introduction

Mental health is an essential component of overall well-being, particularly for students who face continuous academic and social pressures. Despite increasing awareness, existing digital solutions either compromise user privacy or provide only basic tracking without meaningful insights.

Most platforms act as passive record-keeping systems, storing user inputs without analyzing patterns or providing actionable guidance. Additionally, the lack of secure data handling raises concerns regarding confidentiality and misuse of sensitive information.

MindSafe Vault addresses these issues by introducing a secure, intelligent system that not only monitors mental health data but also provides risk detection and controlled doctor-patient interaction while ensuring complete data privacy.

2. Problem Statement

Current mental health systems face several limitations:

• Lack of secure data storage and privacy protection
• Absence of intelligent risk detection mechanisms
• No controlled access between doctor and patient
• Limited insights from recorded mental health data
• Increased user hesitation due to privacy concerns

There is a need for a system that ensures secure storage, intelligent monitoring, and controlled data sharing while maintaining user trust.

3. Proposed System

MindSafe Vault is a secure and intelligent mental health monitoring system that enables:

• Safe recording of mental health data
• Detection of stress patterns using rule-based analysis
• Controlled doctor-patient interaction through permission-based access
• Secure data storage using encryption techniques
• Continuous monitoring and feedback for improved well-being

The system transforms raw user inputs into meaningful insights while ensuring complete confidentiality and control.

