4. System Architecture

The system follows a layered architecture to ensure security, scalability, and modularity.

The Presentation Layer includes user dashboards for patients and doctors, providing interfaces for data entry, record viewing, and interaction.

The Business Logic Layer consists of the Risk Analysis Engine, Decision Rules Engine, and Access Control Manager, responsible for processing data and generating insights.

The Security Layer implements encryption mechanisms and zero-knowledge storage to ensure data confidentiality.

The Data Layer securely stores encrypted records and maintains audit logs for all activities.

This structured architecture ensures clean separation of concerns and supports future scalability.

5. Methodology

The system is developed using a combination of secure design principles and rule-based analysis.

• Secure data handling using encryption techniques
• Rule-based algorithms for stress and risk detection
• Controlled access using permission-based mechanisms
• Continuous monitoring through user data entries
• User-centric design for ease of interaction

The approach emphasizes privacy, accuracy, and usability.

6. Implementation Details

6.1 Data Management Module

Handles:

• Patient record creation
• Continuous data entry (mood, activity, notes)
• Secure record updates

6.2 Risk Analysis Engine

Analyzes:

• Behavioral patterns
• Stress indicators
• Risk levels based on predefined rules

6.3 Access Control System

Manages:

• Doctor access requests
• Patient approval or denial
• Secure data sharing

6.4 Audit System

Maintains:

• Logs of all entries and access
• Tracking of system activities
• Transparency and accountability

